  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Delaware's Mobile Ignition Repair Specialists</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6 leading-snug">
            Professional Ignition Repair Throughout Delaware
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Your ignition is one of the most used mechanical components in your vehicle. Every single time you start your car, the ignition cylinder engages — and over years of daily use, the internal tumblers, springs, and wafers inside can wear, stick, or fail. When that starts to happen, you'll notice the symptoms: a key that feels tight or gritty when turning, a key that requires a little jiggle to engage, or in more advanced cases, a key that simply will not turn at all.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Not every ignition issue requires a full cylinder replacement. Many problems can be resolved with a professional repair — cleaning and lubricating a sticky cylinder, adjusting worn tumblers, or addressing the specific mechanical failure causing the issue. At 1st Capital Locksmith, we diagnose first and recommend repair whenever it is the right solution. We only recommend replacement when repair truly is not sufficient.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            We are fully mobile and serve drivers throughout <a href="/service-areas/dover-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Dover</a>, <a href="/service-areas/milford-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Milford</a>, <a href="/service-areas/smyrna-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Smyrna</a>, <a href="/service-areas/camden-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Camden</a>, <a href="/service-areas/harrington-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Harrington</a>, <a href="/service-areas/frederica-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Frederica</a>, and all surrounding communities in Kent County, Delaware. If your ignition is giving you trouble, call us before it stops working entirely.
          </p>
